(globalThis.CATALOGUE_RECORD_CHUNKS??=Object.create(null))[52]={"source_order":52,"notes":["The superscript after '26' is read as 'b'. Its form is somewhat ambiguous.","Show-through is too faint and reversed to exclude with complete certainty a very faint pencil note on this side. On inspection, no independent writing on this side was identified.","At the far right beyond the gutter (x≈3200–3508) a strip of the facing page fol. 27 is visible. It shows '√C. 163 (' at about [3290,665,220,75]. This belongs to the adjacent page and is not recorded as a target block.","The faint mirrored text visible through the paper is show-through from fol. 26 (verso side). It is not original writing on fol. 26b.","After review of the overview and all six native tiles, the page is a ruled leaf with no catalogue entries. The only writing is the folio number '26b.' at the top-left.","Faint reversed show-through of handwriting from the other side of the leaf is visible across the ruled lines. It is not treated as writing on this page, and no transcription of it is attempted.","Small dark specks occur in the left margin at about [360,1445,30,20] and elsewhere on the page. Nicks and marks run along the gutter edge at about x≈3140–3200. These are physical marks, not text.","At the far right, beyond the gutter (x≈3200–3508), a strip of the facing page, fol. 27 (source order 53), is visible. It shows '√C. 163 (' at about [3290,665,220,75]. This belongs to the adjacent page and is not recorded as a target-page record.","The adjacent fol. 26 (source order 51) closes with the note 'end of extra leaf. Continue at Uttararāmacarita (back)'. This is context only and does not attach any text to this blank page.","The raised letter after '26' has a hooked or angular form. It is read as 'b', which is consistent with the folio label 'fol. 26b', but the letterform alone is not fully secure."],"records":[{"id":"css-prod-0052-r001","local_id":"r001","source_order":52,"folio":"26b","folio_label":"fol. 26b","sequence":1,"page_id":"30d7eab1-f217-40e8-aae1-f2f7273d6a1e","kind":"other","record_type":"non_catalogue_text","source_model_record_type":"non_catalogue_text","subtype":"folio_number","shelfmark":"","titleLiteral":"","titleNormalized":"","displayTitle":"Catalogue text","authorOrSource":"","source":"","subject":"","subjectGroup":"","date":"","extent":"","lines":"","script":"","incipit":"","transcription":"26b.","annotations":["Folio number written at the top-left corner of the page, apparently in pencil or grey ink.","The 'b' is written raised, as a superscript, after '26' and is followed by a point.","A separate small dark dot lies to the right at about [600,350,20,20]. It appears to be a stray mark, not part of the number."],"uncertainties":["The superscript letter after '26' is read as 'b'. Its form is somewhat ambiguous and could be misread as another letter.","The raised letter after '26' has a hooked or angular form. It is read as 'b', which is consistent with the folio label 'fol. 26b', but the letterform alone is not fully secure."],"focused_readings":[],"reviewNotes":[],"editorialNotes":[],"relationships":[],"editorial_context":[],"block_ids":["b001"],"locations":[{"block_id":"b001","bbox":[400,295,135,110]}],"isCancelled":false,"needsReview":true,"human_verified":false,"verification_status":"machine_reviewed","change_audit":[],"sourceCitationURL":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/canvas/30d7eab1-f217-40e8-aae1-f2f7273d6a1e.json","auditPath":"audit/pages/0052.json","attachedNotes":[],"resolvedRelationships":[],"attachedRecords":[]}]};
